I'm not 100% sure about this, but IIRC, if you're confused while
eating, the game won't warn you that you're about to choke.

I just know that I once lost a very promising archaeologist that way: I
had planned to max out strength by eating about 30 lumps of royal
jelly. However, I had forgotten that the damned stuff is pretty
nutritious :(
Well, I suddendly got confused (I guess one of the lumps was rotten),
but I ignored it, ate the next lump and... choked on it. There was no
warning (besides the word "Satiated" on the bottom, should have watched
that status line) and no prompt asking me if I wanted to stop eating. -
DYWYPI?
(FYI, I even had amulets of magical breathing and life saving in my
bag, but happened to be wearing ESP at that time... I bashed my head
against the wall pretty hard after that)

As I said, I'm not sure if it was the confusion that caused it or
something else. But it does make sense that the game won't prevent you
from doing stupid things like that while you're confused.



